# d_isplay: any value as APL2's DISPLAY draws it, as a character matrix
# (B16's marks: an arrow along the top, a down arrow per leading axis,
# a mark at the bottom for what it holds), so a flat array is framed
# too; a simple scalar is itself.
== SOURCE
d_isplay 2 3 r_eshape r_ange 6
d_isplay "abc"
d_isplay "ab" "cde"
s_hape d_isplay 1 2 3
d_isplay 5
== TYPE
Char
Char
Char
Int
Char
== RESULT
┌→────┐
↓1 2 3│
│4 5 6│
└~────┘
┌→──┐
│abc│
└───┘
┌→───────────┐
│ ┌→─┐ ┌→──┐ │
│ │ab│ │cde│ │
│ └──┘ └───┘ │
└∊───────────┘
3 7
5
